      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">Porosity (%)</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">(volume (cm 3 ) ⁇ weight (g)/resin composition density (g/cm 3 ))/volume (cm 3 ) ⁇ 100</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0000">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">Air permeability resistance of a separator comprising a microporous membrane</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was measured using a Gurley type air permeability tester, according to JIS P-8117.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0306">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the average longest pore diameter of the microporous membrane</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was obtained by observing the surface of the microporous membrane with SEM and measuring the pore diameter of the SEM photograph. Specifically, the surface of the microporous membrane was observed by SEM at 30,000 magnification, the longest pore diameters of the micropores within the photograph range of 4.2  ⁇ m ⁇ 3  ⁇ m were measured, and the average value was calculated to obtain the average longest pore diameter. Also, the pore diameter in the longest pore direction and that in the direction perpendicular to the longest pore direction are measured, calculating the average values, dividing the average longest pore diameter by the average value of the pore diameter in the direction perpendicular to the longest pore direction, and then calculating the pore diameter ratio.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0307">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">FIG. 3</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">shows a schematic diagram for illustration of the puncture test conditions and the puncture depth.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0308">
      </li>
