        <span itemprop="subject">the die temperature</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was set to 230° C., and the molten polymer was cooled by blown air and then wound into a roll.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0312">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the extruded precursor</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">(raw film) had a thickness of 15  ⁇ m and then the raw film was annealed at 130° C. for 15 minutes. Next, the annealed film was cold stretched to 21% at room temperature, then hot stretched to 156% at 120° C., and relaxed to 126% at 125° C. to form micropores. Physical properties of the microporous membrane were measured after the aforementioned pore opening upon stretching of the film. The results are shown in Table 5.</span>
